Android 15, internally codenamed "Vanilla Ice Cream," was officially released to AOSP on September 3, 2024, with its rollout to Google Pixel devices beginning on October 15, 2024. This version continued to prioritize privacy, security, and productivity, introducing "Private Space" to securely hide sensitive apps and data, and enhancing theft protection features with AI-powered detection and remote locking capabilities. Android 15 also brought significant improvements for large-screen devices, including a pinnable taskbar and "App Pairs" for efficient split-screen multitasking, alongside new camera controls like "Low Light Boost" for enhanced photography, expanded satellite connectivity for messaging, and OS-level support for app archiving to free up device space.
